    "title": "Re-Asks with Repair Tool Call",
    "description": "### Feature Description\n\nSupport \"re-asks\" with experimental repair tool call. An implementation of re-ask would be to return a tool call result, but with the error (no tool exists, args doesn't match input schema) message attached. https://x.com/lgrammel/status/1865067908214255978\n\nBased on the current implementation, it doesn't seem like it's possible to return a generic object (like in a tool call result), only an actual tool call object: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/core/generate-text/parse-tool-call.ts\n\n\n### Use Cases\n\nInstead of throwing an error, generateText or streamText would \"consume\" a maxStep and try again with the message attached.\n\n### Additional context\n\nIt might be worth deferring input schema validation until the execute method. This is to let parallel tool calls that don't have an error proceed.\n\nRight now for [`generateText`](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/e7a9ec9e916b7cc49e3296d7644be62f9949263c/packages/ai/core/generate-text/generate-text.ts#L385-L408), it's written as\n\n```\ntoolCalls = toolCalls.map(parseToolCalls)\ntoolResults = toolCalls.map(executeToolCalls)\n```\n\nbut maybe it should be\n\n```\ntoolResults = toolCalls.map(executeToolCalls(parseToolCalls))\n```\n\nInstead of throwing an error in `doParseToolCall`, we can set a boolean like `mismatchedArgs`. If the toolName doesn't exist, we could define a wild card fall back tool that developers could provide custom execute method for.\n\nhttps://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/core/generate-text/parse-tool-call.ts
}